<p>North Korean women’s football club Naegohyang FC arrived in South Korea on Sunday for an AFC Women’s Champions League semifinal, the first visit by athletes from North Korea to the South in about eight years. The delegation of 27 players and 12 staff arrived at Incheon International Airport ahead of Wednesday’s match against South Korea’s Suwon FC Women in Suwon. Seoul’s Unification Ministry approved the visit under the inter-Korean exchange law. The permit covers the team’s stay through next weekend, though the club could depart earlier if eliminated. North Korea has described the South as its “most hostile state” and ruled out reunification, while South Korean President Lee Jae Myung has called for improved ties. Naegohyang players did not answer reporters’ questions at the airport and quickly boarded buses under police escort, according to South Korean and Taiwanese reports.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/yUEbHG7LdLRCgkDeoORk-eIAaJPAOrNzp2C_uvvd6pjYmHRqgEs93lHDOLCJnrtYvmjmDuOhXnwu6i8kJ7imfUgfw5M-DSx1FWqDlO2RVNLKmvDauqq9UR8Nu2bTma56f49inRHf7axdAmU2_ExtrBoLeA3kssShNyhkl2WWF2QHycaVKq_Dts-zrTRANXto7HGOLrQu4zlAwC9F-jq_pg' alt='Members of Naegohyang, a North Korean women’s soccer team, arriving at Incheon International Airport in South Korea on Sunday.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Arrival timing: KBS said the team arrived at Incheon International Airport at about 2:20 p.m..</li><li>Arrival scene: CNA said many reporters and civic groups holding welcome signs were at the airport.</li><li>Entry paperwork: Khan reported the players presented passports rather than issued visit certificates.</li><li>Match protocol: Formal training and a news conference were scheduled for the day before the match, according to Yonhap News TV.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Joint cheering organizer: A cheering squad official said the visit showed the possibility of inter-Korean cooperation in multilateral arenas, according to Yonhap. (<a href='https://en.yna.co.kr/view/AEN20260517000300315'>Yonhap News Agency</a>)</li><li>The New York Times: The team’s trip is unlikely to produce a diplomatic thaw by itself, although some sports events have contributed to inter-Korean contacts. (<a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/05/17/world/asia/north-korea-naegohyang-soccer-football.html'>The New York Times</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.dw.com/en/north-korean-women-s-football-team-makes-rare-visit-to-south/a-77186062'>North Korean women&#x27;s football team makes rare visit to South</a> - dw.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/may/17/afc-women-champions-league-north-korea-south-korea-naegohyang-fc-suwon'>‘Tearing down barriers’: North Korean footballers arrive in Seoul for first time in eight years</a> - theguardian.com</li><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/asia/east-asia/article/3353876/north-korean-footballers-arrive-south-match-tickets-sell-out'>North Korean footballers arrive in South, match tickets sell out</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://abcnews.com/International/wireStory/north-korean-womens-soccer-team-arrives-south-korea-133045454'>North Korean women&#x27;s soccer team arrives in South Korea for regional tournament</a> - abcnews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/05/17/world/asia/north-korea-naegohyang-soccer-football.html'>A North Korean Soccer Team Makes a Rare Visit to South Korea</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.enca.com/sport/north-korean-women-footballers-arrive-south-korea-afp'>North Korean women footballers arrive in South Korea: AFP</a> - enca.com</li><li><a href='https://www.bangkokpost.com/sports/3256419/north-korean-women-footballers-arrive-in-south-korea'>North Korean women footballers arrive in South Korea</a> - bangkokpost.com</li><li><a href='http://www.asiaone.com/asia/north-korean-womens-football-club-arrives-south-amid-strained-ties'>North Korean women&#x27;s football club arrives in South amid strained ties</a> - as